    "body": "@annevk I'm not sure what your question is. How does the existing spec work? It works pretty well; just follow the algorithms. (In particular the super-call to [HTMLConstructor] is what creates the element.) But, it fails to add the is=\"\" attribute, as @tkent-google noted.\r\n\r\nI started on this yesterday, but got a bit stuck as there's a clash with the requirement in create-an-element which disallows new attributes being added by the constructor. I'll try again today.",
